│ \x1b[1;38;2;32;140;183mRoot-key escrow\x1b[m                                                                                                      │
│                                                                                                                      │
│ DeviceChain encrypts stored credentials with this instance's root key. Database backups do not contain it. To        │
│ recover after losing the cluster you need this escrow file and its passphrase. Copy the file off this machine; keep  │
│ the passphrase separately.                                                                                           │
│                                                                                                                      │
│   ( ) Write an encrypted escrow file (recommended)                                                                   │
│ › \x1b[7m(*) Do not escrow the root key (--no-escrow)\x1b[m                                                                       │
│                                                                                                                      │
│   \x1b[1;38;2;224;160;48mWARNING: PERMANENT LOSS. Without an escrow file the root key exists only inside the cluster. If the cluster is\x1b[m     │
│   \x1b[1;38;2;224;160;48mlost, every stored secret becomes permanently unreadable, even from a database backup. Choose this only for a\x1b[m      │
│   \x1b[1;38;2;224;160;48mthrowaway instance.\x1b[m                                                                                                │
